<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<!DOCTYPE topic SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/html-entities.dtd">

<topic 
	xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" 
	xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
	title="%cloud% use-cases" id="cloud-use-cases">

    <link-summary>Learn more about use cases where %cloud% can come in handy.</link-summary>

    <chapter id="cloud-use-case-1" title="Get deeper insights into your project trends">

        <p>Using <a href="https://qodana.cloud">%cloud%</a>, you can aggregate %product% reports from various
            projects, explore development trends, and analyze team and project performance.</p>

        <p>To organize your work, %cloud% provides a hierarchy consisting of organizations, teams, and projects.
            These entities let you assign several projects to a single team. Also, you can achieve transparency using
            real-time widgets.</p>

        <p>Each project stores the history of analysis results and compares results between commits. You can examine the
            absolute number of detected problems, or compare the number of problems to a baseline taken during a
            specific Qodana run.</p>

    </chapter>

    <chapter id="cloud-use-case-2" title="Open problems detected by %product% in your favorite IDE">

        <p>If you are already a %product% user, you might know that you can open issues spotted by Qodana right in your IDE.
            This feature is available in %cloud%, so you can fix server-side errors in the editor like other suggestions given by the IDE.</p>

        <p>Using %product%, you can run resource-intensive checks outside your development environment without affecting
            the performance of your IDE. In fact, we created %product% to ensure that you no longer have to choose between code
            quality and IDE performance.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter id="cloud-use-case-3" title="Plan your work better">

        <p>In %cloud%, you can build reports to evaluate all code segments that require modification, and select
            the issues to add to a baseline. This way, the whole team can see the same list of issues and monitor progress
            using the interactive %product% dashboard.</p>
    </chapter>
</topic>
